{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Alas, who shall live when El does this!</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): of these decrees that El places in the world through the king of Assyria, for he defeated all the nations and scattered all the peoples." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'Alas, who shall live when El does this' — concerning Ishmael, for the children of Kenite are of the seed of Ishmael. And what it says, 'for if Cain is set for burning' — that is, if Cain is set for burning fire. And the reason the seed of Ishmael is called Cain is because they dwelt in the inheritance of Cain; and so it says (Judges 4:11): ״וחבר הקיני נפרד מקין״ — 'and Hobab the Kenite had separated from Cain.' Now was it not so that all the children of Cain were cut off in the waters of the Flood? Rather, they were called children of Cain because they dwelt in the inheritance of Cain, and their settlement was the kingdom of Assyria. Balaam said: of all seventy tongues that the Holy One, blessed be He, created in His world, He did not place His name upon any except Israel and Ishmael, as it says (Genesis 16:11): ״וקראת שמו ישמעאל״ — 'and you shall call his name Ishmael.' And since the Holy One, blessed be He, set the name of Ishmael on a par with the name of Israel, 'Alas, who shall live from His name, El' — alas, who shall live in his days. Thus they expounded in Pirkei Rabbi Eliezer." "<b>And if</b> you gain insight you will find that this accuser who is on earth alluded in this verse to the name of the great accuser that Israel has in heaven, and he is the prince of the wilderness, the flying Seraph, the soul-sphere of Mars. For because he saw that he had failed in his counsels and his accusation availed nothing in all his prophecies, neither through the attribute of justice nor through the attribute of mercy, therefore 'he set his face toward the wilderness,' to avail himself of him against Israel. And therefore he began to cry out, 'Who shall live from his decrees' — that is, who shall live in the exile of Esau. And the two vavs allude to his twelve wings; and this is clear."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:55.917747432Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}